2. Star Topology ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Most Important

Definition

In Star Topology, all computers are connected to one central device.

Usually:

Switch
Hub
       PC

        |

PC ---- Switch ---- PC

        |

       PC
How does it work?

Computer A sends data

↓

Switch receives data

↓

Switch sends data only to Computer B

Real-Life Example

Think of a classroom.

Students don't talk to everyone directly.

They communicate through the teacher.

Teacher = Switch

Students = Computers

Advantages
Easy to install
Easy to find faults
Fast
Easy to add new computers
Disadvantages

If the switch fails,

the whole network stops.

Interview Answer

In Star Topology, every computer is connected to a central device like a switch. All communication passes through the switch.

Important Points

✔ Most Popular

✔ Used in Offices

✔ Used in Schools

✔ Used in Colleges

✔ Central Device = Switch
------------------------------------------------------------
3. Ring Topology
Definition

Every computer is connected to two neighboring computers, forming a circle.

PC ------ PC

|         |

PC ------ PC
How does it work?

Data moves

Computer

↓

Computer

↓

Computer

↓

Destination

Real-Life Example

Friends sitting in a circle.

Message passes from one friend to the next.

Advantages
No data collision
Equal access
Disadvantages
One cable failure can stop the network.
Difficult to add new devices.
Interview Answer
Ring Topology connects devices in a circular manner, where each device communicates with its neighboring devices.

Important Points

✔ Circular Structure

✔ One failure may affect communication
----------------------------------------------------------------
4. Mesh Topology
Definition

Every computer is connected to every other computer.

A ------- B

|\      /|

| \    / |

|  \  /  |

D ------- C
How does it work?

If one connection fails,

another path is available.

Real-Life Example

Everyone in your class has everyone's phone number.

If one person doesn't answer,

you contact another person directly.

Advantages
Highly Reliable
Highly Secure
Multiple paths

Disadvantages
Expensive
Lots of cables
Difficult installation
Interview Answer
Mesh Topology connects every device directly to every other device, providing multiple communication paths.

Important Points

✔ Most Reliable

✔ Most Expensive

✔ Used in Military

✔ Used in Data Centers

5. Tree Topology
Definition
Tree Topology is a combination of multiple Star Topologies arranged in a hierarchy.

        Main Switch

        /       \

    Switch     Switch

    /   \       /   \

   PC   PC    PC   PC
Real-Life Example

Company

↓

Department

↓

Employees

Advantages
Easy to expand
Easy management
Disadvantages

If the main switch fails,

many devices lose connection.

Interview Answer
Tree Topology is a hierarchical topology formed by connecting multiple Star networks.

Important Points

✔ Hierarchical Structure
✔ Used in Large Organizations
--------------------------------------
6. Hybrid Topology
Definition
Hybrid Topology is a combination of two or more topologies.

Example:

Star + Bus

Star + Ring

Real-Life Example

A company may use:

Star Topology in one department.
Ring Topology in another department.

Together they form a Hybrid Topology.

Advantages
Flexible
Scalable
Reliable
Disadvantages
Expensive
Complex design
Interview Answer
Hybrid Topology combines two or more different network topologies into one network.

Important Points

✔ Used in Big Companies

✔ Combination of Multiple Topologies

